-- title:
--   Minimal primes of (p) on the pole chart of X_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$; assume the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` (namely $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNum` over $\mathbb{Q}$) lies in the intermediate field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral-form ratios for $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a model structure `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of the function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` pinned by the Gauss condition: $f_0 \in W_0$ exactly when there are power series $a,a'$ over the subring of rationals with denominator coprime to $p$ such that $a'$ has nonzero reduction modulo $p$ and $f_0 \cdot a' = a$ as Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$. Then there is a family $P : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to$ ideals of the pole-chart algebra `chartAlgInf p (ΓM M H) hj` (the subalgebra of the function field generated over `R p` by $j^{-1}$) such that each $P_i$ is a minimal prime of the ideal generated by $p$, $P_0 \ne P_1$, the set of minimal primes of $(p)$ is exactly $\{P_0,P_1\}$, an element $b$ lies in $P_0$ precisely when its image in the function field is a nonunit of $W_0$, and, for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit in $A$ and with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, every ring map $\rho : R\,p \to A$ whose composite with the inclusion of $A$ is the structure map $R\,p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $i \in \{0,1\}$, every point $y$ of the fibre of the model along the residue map $\overline{\rho}$, and every prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of the pole-chart algebra whose image under `ιInf` agrees with the image of $y$ under the first projection: $y$ lies in the range of the base map of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ i` if and only if $P_i \subseteq \mathfrak{q}$.
--
--   This records the structure of the special fibre at $p$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ when $p$ exactly divides $M$, read on the chart at the cusps ($j^{-1}$-chart): the fibre has exactly two components, identified with the two minimal primes of $(p)$ in the chart ring, oriented so that the zeroth one is cut out by the Gauss valuation, and the identification is saturated in the sense that membership of a geometric fibre point in a component is equivalent to containment of the corresponding branch prime. It is the pole-chart counterpart of the analogous statement on the finite chart, and is used in the results distinguishing the two sides of the fibre at cuspidal points.
